hallenge. The latest official inventory identifies more than 2,600 federal programs covering $7 trillion in spending, yet even this list is incomplete. Across a federal government this expansive overlap is inevitable because multiple programs often pursue the same objectives or provide similar services to the same beneficiaries.  Programs accumulate over decades as Congress responds to new priorities without always rev, Author(s): Seth Doer, Demian Brady"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},